{
  "_id": "fhSubIronHour001",
  "name": "Ironhour Caps",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Sealed glass vials of black-coated capsules sold under counter as \"jobsite supplements.\" The label is a knockoff of a defunct legitimate brand. Used by movers, longshoremen, and the desperate.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks and your carrying capacity is doubled.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Ironhour Caps (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Ironhour Caps.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws (your reflexes feel a half-second slow).</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw; on a failed save, you suffer withdrawal for 3 days. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check and make the saving throw. While in withdrawal, abstaining takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances.</em></p>"
    },
